fact WorkItem(id: "WI-502", description: some(value: "Typed terms and rules — deep re-engineering of the Term/resolution representation so a term (and a rule's head/body) carries its type, enabling type-directed reasoning (esp. [simp] firing, proposal 043 §4) to READ the type rather than re-derive it. Motivation: WI-283 made [simp] firing type-directed but split it across two sites — the typer has typed occurrences (NodeOccurrence.inferred_type, WI-284) and fires requires-guarded rules via simp_fire_guard_holds (typing.rs); the resolver holds type-erased Terms and so skips them (equation_is_requires_guarded, resolve.rs). Converging the two (WI-292) needs the resolver to know each term's type. Re-deriving it structurally is REJECTED (a second notion of type that can drift from the typer); reusing NodeOccurrence is wrong (occurrence = source-code form, not the resolution carrier). So the type must live on the term/value carrier itself, populated ONCE at the typing boundary and carried through resolution without recomputation. Scope/design (TBD in this WI): where the type slot lives (Value at eval/value.rs is unboxed/zero-alloc — don't bloat scalars), how it is populated at the source->resolver boundary (incl. typing rule bodies / the simplify-prove entry, which are untyped today), and how it is preserved through De Bruijn opening + substitution (where inferred_type is currently dropped). Clients: WI-292 (resolver-side type-directed firing) and WI-283's typer firing become clients of one typed substrate. Acceptance: terms carry types accessible during resolution such that a requires-guarded [simp] rule can fire on the resolver/prove path by reading the carried type (no re-derivation); cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-569"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-08T19:52:28Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "claude", content: "Design specced 2026-06-26 in docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md (committed 18471bc): a CONSTRAINT substrate of which type is one kind, carrier-centric; untyped kernel by stratification; type-specificity = an untyped guard over type-terms; type caches on the carrier (never the shared TermId); functional model kept (explicit wakeup, no cells). Two shapes (A monomorphize at boundary, B guard over the type that flows from the redex). Staged Step0..6; check+suspend now, label later. Step 0 (persistent imbl substitution, O(1) frame.subst.clone) = WI-569, DELIVERED (commit 18471bc).", at: "2026-06-26T11:52:25Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "user", content: "Staged Steps 0-6 now filed as tracking WIs (tag wi502): Step 0 = WI-569 (DELIVERED, persistent imbl subst); Step 1 = WI-570 (DELIVERED 8fe8977 — tagged persistent constraint store, lacks=kind#1 / Type=kind#2, residual C on the answer, write-mostly); Step 2 = WI-571 (carry+wakeup choke-point bind path); Step 3 = WI-572 (static type on carrier + min_sort read API); Step 4 = WI-573 (Shape A monomorphization, unblocks WI-567/WI-566); Step 5 = WI-292 (Shape B guard firing in resolver, the umbrella acceptance); Step 6 = WI-574 (generative labeling, PreOpened/deferred). Chain: 569→570→571→572→{573, 292}; 573→{567,566}; 292→574. This umbrella completes when Step 5 (WI-292) lands.", at: "2026-06-26T13:22:02Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "claude", content: "PIVOT 2026-06-27: type-directed firing is TYPER-SIDE (compile-time), not resolver-side. Monomorphization (Shape A) dropped — it cannot name an abstract carrier instance and only solved the redundant concrete sub-case. Single mechanism: the typer reads the carried type (Step 3 min_sort_of_value), checks subsort(min_sort(?x), Spec) — an ABSTRACT carrier resolved via the Step-1 constraint store (requires Spec[A]) — and fires the [simp] at load; the resolver stays type-blind, no runtime type-directed rewrite (runtime concrete values are value-directed by eval). Steps re-scoped: Step 4 = WI-292 (rule bodies), Step 5 = WI-573 (guarded-effect guards, was Shape A). Umbrella acceptance reframed: a requires-guarded [simp] fires AT THE TYPER by reading the carried type. See revised docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md.", at: "2026-06-27T06:42:42Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "claude", content: "CORRECTION 2026-06-27 (supersedes the prior PIVOT feedback): design merged + converged in docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md (now 'Typed terms'; typed-term-carrier.md folded into it). Model: typing is typed(untyped-value, env) -> typed-value, run ONCE at the boundary, env = the SOURCE of type info; min_sort / min_sort_of_value REMOVED (a source-less pull that returned None on constructed values). A value carries its CONCRETE type (typed value -> runtime monomorphization at dispatch); a logical variable carries its type as a CONSTRAINT (typed variable -> checking; the Step-1 store). Structural kernel (discrim/unify/match/subst) stays type-blind; type-rule machinery rides above, reading the carried type. Relation = facts/SLD; unification + typing process = Rust (SLD planned). WI-502 REMAINING work = typed-VALUE carrier ((type,TermId) pair for Value::Term) + typed(value,env) boundary op + remove min_sort + resolver machinery for typed rule patterns (?x: T syntax + match reading the carried type). Steps 1-3 (WI-570/571/572) = the typed-VARIABLE half, delivered. WI-292 ([simp] firing), WI-573 (guard discharge), runtime monomorphization = CONSUMERS (dependents), not steps. DROPPED: Shape A / Shape B and the brief typer-side-firing re-scope.", at: "2026-06-27T08:08:30Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-502", author: "claude", content: "DELIVERED 2026-07-08 (umbrella). Acceptance MET on both halves: (1) cargo-test GREEN — full workspace suite 2643 passed / 0 failed / exit 0 (rustland/scripts/test.sh); (2) a requires-guarded [simp] rule fires on the resolver/prove path by READING the carried type, no re-derivation — WI-292, tests resolver_fires_requires_guarded_equation_when_carrier_provides_spec (op2(5,7)->5 since Int64 provides Magma) + resolver_does_not_fire_..._when_carrier_lacks_spec (op2(true,false) intact, Bool lacks Magma). Whole staged chain delivered: Steps 0-3 typed-VARIABLE half (WI-569/570/571/572), typed-VALUE carrier + typed(value,env) + min_sort removed (WI-578), typed rule pattern syntax ?x:T / [T] introducer (WI-582), firing consumer WI-292, guard discharge WI-573, prereqs/guardrails/phases WI-581/584/592/595/596/611. ONLY non-delivered wi502 item = WI-574 generative labeling, PreOpened/DEFERRED BY DESIGN (docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md: 'check + suspend ships first; generative labeling is deferred, opt-in, same representation') — a separate future capability, NOT umbrella acceptance. Documented WI-582 follow-ons (typer-side enforcement of typed-rule bounds — the typer currently SKIPS typed rules, sound-but-conservative; printer round-trip of ?x:T; compound multi-var bounds) are enhancements outside acceptance, unfiled. No code changed this session — repo was at the delivered committed state; verification-only.", at: "2026-07-08T19:52:21Z")
